# 基础词 Unit11
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 基础词Unit11核心词汇

{{journal}}{{/ˈdʒɜːnl}}{{n. 日志；期刊}}{{She published her research in a scientific journal.}}
{{journalist}}{{/ˈdʒɜːnəlɪst}}{{n. 记者；新闻工作者}}{{The journalist reported on the political crisis.}}
{{journey}}{{/ˈdʒɜːni}}{{n. 旅程；过程}}{{The journey from Beijing to Shanghai takes five hours by train.}}
{{judge}}{{/dʒʌdʒ}}{{n./v. 法官；判断}}{{Don't judge a book by its cover.}}
{{juice}}{{/dʒuːs}}{{n. 果汁}}{{She ordered a glass of orange juice.}}
{{jump}}{{/dʒʌmp}}{{v./n. 跳跃；猛增}}{{The cat jumped onto the table.}}
{{junior}}{{/ˈdʒuːniər}}{{adj./n. 初级的；年少者}}{{He is a junior employee in the company.}}
{{jury}}{{/ˈdʒʊəri}}{{n. 陪审团}}{{The jury reached a unanimous verdict.}}
{{justice}}{{/ˈdʒʌstɪs}}{{n. 正义；公正；司法}}{{The pursuit of justice is a fundamental right.}}
{{justify}}{{/ˈdʒʌstɪfaɪ}}{{v. 证明…正当；为…辩护}}{{How can you justify spending so much money?}}
{{keen}}{{/kiːn}}{{adj. 热衷的；敏锐的}}{{She is keen on learning new languages.}}
{{key}}{{/kiː}}{{n./adj. 钥匙；关键的}}{{Education is the key to a better future.}}
{{keyboard}}{{/ˈkiːbɔːd}}{{n. 键盘}}{{He types quickly on the keyboard.}}
{{kid}}{{/kɪd}}{{n. 小孩；年轻人}}{{The kids were playing in the park.}}
{{kingdom}}{{/ˈkɪŋdəm}}{{n. 王国；领域}}{{The animal kingdom is incredibly diverse.}}
{{kneel}}{{/niːl}}{{v. 跪下}}{{She knelt down to pick up the fallen coins.}}
{{knit}}{{/nɪt}}{{v. 编织；紧密结合}}{{She knitted a scarf for her grandson.}}
{{knock}}{{/nɒk}}{{v./n. 敲；敲击}}{{Someone knocked on the door loudly.}}
{{knot}}{{/nɒt}}{{n./v. 结；节；打结}}{{He tied the rope in a tight knot.}}
{{knowledge}}{{/ˈnɒlɪdʒ}}{{n. 知识；了解}}{{Knowledge is power.}}
{{label}}{{/ˈleɪbl}}{{n./v. 标签；贴标签}}{{Read the label carefully before taking the medicine.}}
{{labor}}{{/ˈleɪbər}}{{n. 劳动；劳力}}{{The company relies on cheap labor.}}
{{lack}}{{/læk}}{{n./v. 缺乏；不足}}{{The project failed due to a lack of funding.}}
{{landscape}}{{/ˈlændskeɪp}}{{n. 风景；景色}}{{The landscape in Guilin is breathtaking.}}
{{lane}}{{/leɪn}}{{n. 小路；车道；泳道}}{{Stay in the right lane while driving on the highway.}}
{{lap}}{{/læp}}{{n. 膝部；一圈}}{{The cat sat on her lap while she read.}}
{{launch}}{{/lɔːntʃ}}{{v./n. 发射；启动；推出}}{{The company launched a new smartphone last week.}}
{{laundry}}{{/ˈlɔːndri}}{{n. 洗衣房；待洗的衣服}}{{She did the laundry on Sunday morning.}}
{{layer}}{{/ˈleɪər}}{{n. 层；层次}}{{The cake has three layers of chocolate.}}
{{layout}}{{/ˈleɪaʊt}}{{n. 布局；设计}}{{The layout of the office is very efficient.}}
{{lead}}{{/liːd}}{{v./n. 领导；引导；铅}}{{She leads a team of 20 researchers.}}
{{lean}}{{/liːn}}{{v./adj. 倾斜；瘦的}}{{He leaned against the wall to rest.}}
{{leap}}{{/liːp}}{{v./n. 跳跃；飞跃}}{{The frog leaped into the pond.}}
{{lecture}}{{/ˈlektʃər}}{{n./v. 讲座；讲课}}{{The professor gave a lecture on modern history.}}
{{legal}}{{/ˈliːɡl}}{{adj. 法律的；合法的}}{{It is illegal to drive without a license.}}
{{legend}}{{/ˈledʒənd}}{{n. 传说；传奇人物}}{{The legend of Robin Hood is well known in England.}}
{{leisure}}{{/ˈleʒər}}{{n. 休闲；空闲}}{{She spends her leisure time reading and gardening.}}
{{length}}{{/leŋθ}}{{n. 长度；时间长短}}{{The length of the bridge is 500 meters.}}
{{liberal}}{{/ˈlɪbərəl}}{{adj. 自由的；开明的}}{{She holds liberal views on social issues.}}
{{liberate}}{{/ˈlɪbəreɪt}}{{v. 解放；释放}}{{The country was liberated after years of struggle.}}
{{liberty}}{{/ˈlɪbəti}}{{n. 自由；自由权}}{{Liberty is a fundamental human right.}}
{{license}}{{/ˈlaɪsns}}{{n. 许可证；执照}}{{You need a license to drive a car.}}
{{lieutenant}}{{/lefˈtenənt}}{{n. 中尉；副职}}{{The lieutenant led his soldiers into battle.}}
{{limit}}{{/ˈlɪmɪt}}{{n./v. 限制；限度}}{{There is a speed limit of 60 km/h in this area.}}
{{line}}{{/laɪn}}{{n. 线；行；排队}}{{Please stand in line and wait your turn.}}
{{link}}{{/lɪŋk}}{{n./v. 链接；联系}}{{The report links smoking to lung cancer.}}
{{liquid}}{{/ˈlɪkwɪd}}{{n./adj. 液体；液态的}}{{Water is a clear liquid at room temperature.}}
{{list}}{{/lɪst}}{{n./v. 列表；列出}}{{She made a list of things to buy.}}
{{literature}}{{/ˈlɪtrətʃər}}{{n. 文学；文献}}{{She has a deep love for English literature.}}
{{load}}{{/ləʊd}}{{n./v. 负荷；装载}}{{The truck was loaded with goods.}}
{{loan}}{{/ləʊn}}{{n./v. 贷款；借出}}{{She took out a loan to buy a house.}}
{{local}}{{/ˈləʊkl}}{{adj./n. 当地的；本地人}}{{The local government built a new hospital.}}
{{locate}}{{/ləʊˈkeɪt}}{{v. 位于；找到}}{{The hotel is located near the beach.}}
{{lock}}{{/lɒk}}{{n./v. 锁；锁上}}{{Don't forget to lock the door when you leave.}}
{{log}}{{/lɒɡ}}{{n./v. 原木；日志；记录}}{{He chopped the log into firewood.}}
{{logical}}{{/ˈlɒdʒɪkl}}{{adj. 逻辑的；合理的}}{{Your argument is logical and well-supported.}}
{{lonely}}{{/ˈləʊnli}}{{adj. 孤独的；寂寞的}}{{She felt lonely after her friends moved away.}}
{{loose}}{{/luːs}}{{adj. 松的；宽松的}}{{The screw was loose and needed tightening.}}
{{loss}}{{/lɒs}}{{n. 损失；丧失}}{{The company suffered heavy losses last year.}}
{{lovely}}{{/ˈlʌvli}}{{adj. 可爱的；令人愉快的}}{{The garden looks lovely in spring.}}
{{lower}}{{/ˈləʊər}}{{adj./v. 较低的；降低}}{{The company decided to lower the prices.}}
{{loyal}}{{/ˈlɔɪəl}}{{adj. 忠诚的；忠实的}}{{He has been a loyal friend for many years.}}
{{luggage}}{{/ˈlʌɡɪdʒ}}{{n. 行李}}{{Please collect your luggage at the carousel.}}
{{lump}}{{/lʌmp}}{{n. 块；肿块}}{{She put a lump of sugar in her tea.}}
{{lung}}{{/lʌŋ}}{{n. 肺}}{{Smoking can cause serious lung diseases.}}
{{luxury}}{{/ˈlʌkʃəri}}{{n./adj. 奢侈品；豪华的}}{{The hotel offers luxury accommodation.}}
